Hand-written from the documented shapes of two OpenAI APIs and the types of the installed
`openai` package (7.57.0). None of these files is a recording: no live call has been made
(the key on the machine that wrote them was expired). Replace them with recorded traffic
when a valid key is available.

Speech to text — POST /v1/audio/transcriptions with `stream: true`
guide https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/speech-to-text (Streaming)
SDK types resources/audio/transcriptions.d.ts: TranscriptionCreateParamsStreaming,
TranscriptionTextDeltaEvent, TranscriptionTextDoneEvent

transcription.sse the server-sent events of one transcription: three
`transcript.text.delta` events and the `transcript.text.done` that
carries the whole text
transcription-truncated.sse the same stream cut off before `transcript.text.done`
error-429.json a rate-limit error body
error-400.json an invalid-request error body

Text to speech — the Realtime API over a WebSocket, wss://api.openai.com/v1/realtime?model=…
guides https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/realtime-websocket
https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/realtime-conversations
SDK types resources/realtime/realtime.d.ts: SessionUpdateEvent,
ConversationItemCreateEvent, ResponseCreateEvent, ResponseAudioDeltaEvent
(`response.output_audio.delta`), ResponseDoneEvent, RealtimeErrorEvent

realtime-speech.jsonl the server events of one spoken response, one JSON object per
line, in the order the server sends them: session.created,
session.updated, response.created, two
response.output_audio.delta events (base64 of 8 and 4 bytes of
PCM), response.output_audio.done, response.done (completed)
realtime-failed.jsonl a response that ends with status `failed` and a server_error
realtime-error.jsonl an `error` event for an invalid request
